  "notes": "Waiver filing, cash basis (Exhibit A). General and Street columns governmental; Enterprise Fund column business-type (beginning 6,009 + State Receipts: Other 269,174 + transfer in 6,002 - Capital Improvements 275,452 = 5,733). Mixed rows (State Receipts: Other, Capital Improvements, Transfers In) split by fund column. Solid Waste 5,262, Water 5,986 and Debt Service 5,497 are printed in the General Fund column, so kept governmental per column (as FY2023). Governmental cash = line 3/28 subtotals (net cash + Street investments), roll-forward 54,595 + 49,206 - 49,502 = 54,299. Transfers (schedule p5): General to Street 2,140 and General to Enterprise 6,002 (total 8,142); governmental transfers_in = Street 2,140, transfers_out = General 8,142, business transfers_net +6,002. Capital Improvements has no printed function, so labelled 'Capital Outlay', detail_category not itemized. Pages 2 and 4 (pages 1a/2a) are blank continuation columns. Outstanding NDEE sewer/lagoon debt 116,389.46 (p5) is not on the cash statement, so no liabilities. Investments: CD 5,102 (Street Fund; beginning 5,085). County treasurer balances 37.52 / 20.14 printed below the statement, not in the roll-forward. No other detail schedules; detail is per fund column from Exhibit A. Read pages 1-5 of 5"
